loadWorkbench: read current live definition and render tool buttons in declared order.
runWorkbenchTool: open a built-in browser tool, inspect a target, or perform a typed object call and expose its reusable result.
open/save/resetWorkbench: open the visual editor with JSON mode, save validated drafts through ordinary messages, restore defaults and inspect the owner object.
openExamples/selectExample: read catalog, preserve per-example browser drafts and populate editable text controls.
saveExample: atomically update all documentation text through one native method.
runExample: save changes, execute source and check, display status/transcript and reusable typed result.
resetExample: replace the selected example's scratch workspace.
newExample: add an editable initial example returning 42.
inspectExample: open the example or its workspace as an ordinary object.


Render saved tool order in the sidebar, attach action metadata for styling, display the configured workbench name in the header and retain all existing action dispatch.


Filter examples by title, description and source; show an empty state. Display a saved observed result and explicit Use observed result as check action. Empty checks report completion without a pass claim. Reset restores the captured example bindings.

Services and Shared session tool actions open their respective panels.
